/*
Name: Walter Shields
Date: mm/dd/yyyy
Description: Aggregate Funtions |  WHat are our all times Global sales?

WSDA Music - Formatted Staff Contact List

WSDA Music's office manager needs a clean staff contact list for the internal company directory. She needs each employee's name in a consistent format: last name in uppercase followed by a comma and their first name; alongside their standardized lowercase email address and job title.

Your job is to use SQL string functions to produce this formatted list for WSDA Music internal company directory.

Result:
Your output should contain 3 columns and 8 rows:
- StaffName - last name in UPPERCASE, comma, then first name (e.g. ADAMS, Andrew)
- EmailAddress - email address in all lowercase
- Title - the employee's job title
Requirements:
- Select from the Employee table
- Use UPPER on LastName
- Use || to concatenate the name: UPPER(LastName) || ', ' || FirstName
- Use LOWER on Email
- Sort results alphabetically by LastName
- Include a comment stating the purpose of the query
*/

SELECT
UPPER(LastName) || ',' || FirstName AS StaffName,
 LOWER(Email) AS EmailAddress,
 Title
FROM 
Employee

ORDER BY 
LastName 
</sql><current_tab id="0"/></tab_sql></sqlb_project>
